{
  "id": "Lyo.Query.Postgres",
  "name": "Lyo.Query.Postgres",
  "area": "Data",
  "tagline": "Translate Lyo.Query Fuzzy operators to Postgres pg_trgm similarity() on IQueryable.",
  "description": "PostgreSQL adapter for [`Lyo.Query`](../Lyo.Query/README.md). `AddLyoQueryPostgres()` replaces `IWhereClauseService` with `PostgresWhereClauseService`, which rewrites `FuzzyMatch.Similarity` calls to `EF.Functions.TrigramsSimilarity` so Npgsql emits SQL `similarity(col, query) >= threshold`.\n\nThe evaluator stays EF-agnostic: in-memory matchers and `EnumerableQuery` keep the CLR Jaccard implementation. SQL Fuzzy requires `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pg_trgm` once per database. GIN/GiST `gin_trgm_ops` indexes are not created by this package.\n\nTargets `net10.0`. Call after `AddLyoQueryServices()`.",
  "features": [
    "**SQL Fuzzy / NotFuzzy.** `similarity()` via Npgsql `EF.Functions.TrigramsSimilarity`, with a per-condition threshold (default 0.3).",
    "**CLR fallback.** `EnumerableQuery`, `MatchesWhereClause`, and `ExplainMatch` keep `FuzzyMatch.Similarity` so they do not pull the table into memory.",
    "**Opt-in DI.** `AddLyoQueryPostgres()` `Replace`s `IWhereClauseService`. Without it, Fuzzy on EF fails translation instead of silently scanning."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register after Lyo.Query",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "using Lyo.Query;\nusing Lyo.Query.Postgres;\n\nservices.AddLocalCache(/* … */);\nservices.AddLyoQueryServices();\nservices.AddLyoQueryPostgres();\n\n// Database (once): CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pg_trgm;"
    },
    {
      "title": "Fuzzy where clause",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "var where = WhereClauseBuilder.And()\n    .Fuzzy(\"Name\", \"jon\", threshold: 0.4)\n    .Build();\n\nvar filtered = whereClauseService.ApplyWhereClause(db.People, where);"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "Indexes",
      "body": "The `%` operator can use a GIN/GiST `gin_trgm_ops` index more readily than `similarity() >= n`. v1 emits `similarity()` so mixed per-condition thresholds in one tree stay correct. Add `CREATE INDEX … USING gist (lower(name) gist_trgm_ops)` on hot columns if you own the schema; this package does not."
    }
  ],
